<page "theming" notebook>
	<header level="1">
		Theming
		<header>Tokens, layers, the app stylesheet and Fomantic's themes: restyle everything from CSS.</>
	</>

	<!--
		THEMING:  the old `theming.mdx` (tokens, layers, remaps, the app stylesheet, themes) in Fomantic's
		`usage/theming.html.eco` order (Preface, Using Themes, Composing a Component, Cascading Inheritance), plus a live
		theme gallery (`<ui-theme-menu>` over sample components), the foundation's token tables (`<ui-docs-tokens global>`)
		and the porting recipe from `guides/ui/notes/theming.md`.
	-->
	<section label="Preface">
		<markdown>
			Spell UI styles everything from CSS custom properties, the **tokens**. They inherit into every component's shadow
			root, so theming is mostly a matter of setting a few of them: say how your look DIFFERS from the default, never
			re-describe the whole thing. Fomantic calls this "progressive truthfulness"; its LESS variables become our tokens,
			and its packaged themes become token sheets you switch at runtime.

			- The default look is neutral: the platform's own UI font, a 16px base and an OKLCH palette that works in light
			  AND dark mode.
			- **Classic** restores Fomantic's original look (Lato, 14px, Fomantic's palette), and every theme is a delta on
			  top of it:  Spell's own ten, **Spell**, **Glass**, **Fruity**, **Merlot**, **Paper**, **Midnight**, **Crisp**, **Pop**, **Matrix** and **Mockup**.
			- Fomantic's own themes were ported too, and are archived (`src/styles/themes/archive/`):  kept only to copy
			  from, in no menu and no bundle.
			- Everything lives in `src/styles/`; the design notes are in `guides/ui/notes/theming.md`.
		</>
	</>

