	<section label="Using themes">
		<section label="Sitewide defaults" sticky="stack" collapsible dividing>
			<example "Sitewide defaults" description="Every colour derives from a few base tokens: re-point `--ui-primary` or a hue's per-scheme base, and its hover, focus, down and active states, its text, border and background roles follow. Edit a value below to try it on these buttons.">
				<html>
					<ui-docs-tokens global playground tokens="--ui-primary --ui-secondary --ui-red --ui-green --ui-blue --ui-radius">
						<ui-button color="primary">Primary Button</ui-button>
						<ui-button color="secondary">Secondary Button</ui-button>
						<ui-button color="red">Red</ui-button>
						<ui-button color="green">Green</ui-button>
						<ui-button color="blue">Blue</ui-button>
					</ui-docs-tokens>
				</html>
				<message slot="description" state="info" size="small">These tokens are Fomantic's site variables (<text code>@primaryColor</text>, <text code>@red</text> ...). A hue's base is a light-dark() pair of tokens:  re-colour both, <text code>--ui-red-on-light</text> and <text code>--ui-red-on-dark</text>, to keep dark mode.</message>
			</example>
		</>
		<markdown>
			```css
			@layer ui.app {
			  :root {
			    --ui-primary: var(--ui-pink);
			    --ui-primary-inverted: var(--ui-pink-inverted);
			    --ui-secondary: var(--ui-grey);
			    --ui-red-on-light: oklch(0.58 0.22 20);
			    --ui-red-on-dark: oklch(0.72 0.17 20);
			  }
			}
			```
		</>

		<!-- GAP I57:  no public token for the chosen box's background / border, so Fomantic's branded checkbox can't come from tokens alone. -->
		<section label="Component defaults" sticky="stack" collapsible dividing>
			<example "Component defaults" description="Components inherit the global tokens and redefine what's theirs in public `--ui-<tag>-*` tokens, e.g. checkboxes in your brand colour instead of grey. Each component page lists its tokens on its Theming tab.">
				<html>
					<ui-docs-tokens family="ui-checkbox" playground tokens="--ui-checkbox-mark-color --ui-checkbox-border-color --ui-checkbox-radius --ui-checkbox-toggle-lane-on --ui-checkbox-slider-line-on">
						<ui-checkbox selected>Checkbox</ui-checkbox>
						<ui-radio name="theming-radio" value="a" selected>A</ui-radio>
						<ui-radio name="theming-radio" value="b">B</ui-radio>
						<ui-checkbox appearance="slider" selected>Slider</ui-checkbox>
						<ui-checkbox appearance="toggle" selected>Toggle</ui-checkbox>
					</ui-docs-tokens>
				</html>
			</example>
		</>

		<section label="Applying a theme" sticky="stack" collapsible dividing>
			<markdown>
				A theme is a sheet of token overrides plus class-grammar rules in `@layer ui.theme`. `UI.themes` (the runtime) loads it and
				applies it on the page AND in every component's shadow root, existing and future:
			</>
			<markdown>
				```js
				import { UI } from "spell/ui/core"

				const { themes } = await UI.load() // `UI.themes` is there once the runtime has loaded
				themes.own // ["spell", "glass", "fruity", "merlot"]:  Spell's own themes, on top of classic
				await themes.apply("spell") // classic + spell:  the Spell brand look
				await themes.apply("merlot") // classic + merlot, on the page and in every shadow root
				await themes.apply("classic") // classic alone
				await themes.apply(undefined) // our own look
				```
			</>
			<markdown>
				- Each sheet is its own lazy chunk, loaded on the first `apply()`; concurrent calls: the last one wins.
				- Under it, `UI.styles.register(name, css, { page: true, shadow: true })` adopts the sheet into the document and
				  every shadow root, after the utilities and before the app stylesheet.
				- A page without the runtime can still `<link>` `ui.css` + `themes/classic.css` + `themes/<name>.css`, but then
				  only the TOKEN half reaches components: the class-grammar overrides need the runtime's shadow adoption.
				- `<ui-theme-menu>` is the theme menu, on this site and every Spell page: Spell's four themes and a light / dark /
				  system switch, both remembered per viewer ([its page](/theme-menu)).
			</>
			<message size="small" class="site-not-ported">Not ported: Fomantic's per-component <text code>theme.config</> (a different packaged theme for each component) -- one theme applies to the whole page; mix looks by setting component tokens, or by copying a theme's rules for one component into your app stylesheet.</>
		</>

		<section label="Dark mode" sticky="stack" collapsible dividing>
			<markdown>
				Dark mode follows the OS by default (`color-scheme: light dark` on `:root`, in `ui.tokens`, so a page's own
				`color-scheme` wins). Every colour token is a `light-dark()` pair resolved where it's USED, so forcing a scheme on
				any subtree flips every colour below it, through shadow boundaries.

				- `class="ui-dark"` / `class="ui-light"` force a scheme on a subtree; `ui-invert` flips relative to its parent.
				- `themes/dark.css` forces dark page-wide; a light-only page sets `:root { color-scheme: light }`.
				- `<ui-root theme="dark">` does the same for everything inside a root, on top of any theme.
			</>

			<section label="A dark region" sticky="stack" collapsible dividing>
				<example "A dark region" description="`ui-dark` forces the dark scheme on a subtree:  every token below it flips.">
					<segment class="ui-dark">
						<header level="4">Dark, whatever the page scheme</header>
						<button color="primary">Primary</button>
						<label color="blue">Blue text re-resolves too</label>
					</segment>
				</example>
			</>
		</>
	</>

	<section label="Composing a component">
		<section label="The pieces" sticky="stack" collapsible dividing>
			<markdown>
				Fomantic composes a component from a definition (`.less`) plus a theme's `.variables` and `.overrides`. Ours is a
				shadow-root sheet per component (`UIButton.css`, a port of the `.less`) over these foundation sheets:
			</>
			<table celled padding="compact" appearance="striped">
				<row header>
					<cell>Sheet</>
					<cell>What</>
					<cell>Layer</>
				</>
				<row>
					<cell>
						<text code>layers.css</>
					</>
					<cell>the layer order; MUST be first in every tree scope</>
					<cell>--</>
				</>
				<row>
					<cell>
						<text code>reset.css</>
					</>
					<cell>box-sizing / margin reset for shadow markup (<text code>:host</>-scoped, never touches the page)</>
					<cell>
						<text code>ui.reset</>
					</>
				</>
				<row>
					<cell><text code>tokens.css</> *</>
					<cell>type, spacing, radii, borders, ink, shadows, motion, z-index, breakpoints</>
					<cell>
						<text code>ui.tokens</>
					</>
				</>
				<row>
					<cell><text code>colors.css</> *</>
					<cell>palette, semantic and neutral colours, colour remaps, colour utilities</>
					<cell><text code>ui.tokens</>, <text code>ui.utilities</></>
				</>
				<row>
					<cell><text code>sizes.css</> *</>
					<cell>size ratios, size remaps, font-size and spacing utilities</>
					<cell><text code>ui.tokens</>, <text code>ui.utilities</></>
				</>
				<row>
					<cell>
						<text code>animations.css</>
					</>
					<cell>the transition catalogue and its hooks</>
					<cell>
						<text code>ui.utilities</>
					</>
				</>
				<row>
					<cell>
						<text code>utilities.css</>
					</>
					<cell>layout / text / theme / visibility utilities (<link link="/utilities">Utilities</>)</>
					<cell>
						<text code>ui.utilities</>
					</>
				</>
				<row>
					<cell>
						<text code>typography.css</>
					</>
					<cell>page typography, opt-in with <text code>class="ui-typography"</></>
					<cell>
						<text code>ui.base</>
					</>
				</>
				<row>
					<cell>
						<text code>native.css</>
					</>
					<cell>native markup slotted into components, CSS-only tooltips, <text code>ui-native</></>
					<cell>
						<text code>ui.components</>
					</>
				</>
				<row>
					<cell>
						<text code>themes/classic.css</>
					</>
					<cell>Fomantic's original look</>
					<cell>
						<text code>ui.theme</>
					</>
				</>
				<row>
					<cell>
						<text code>themes/dark.css</>
					</>
					<cell>force the dark scheme page-wide</>
					<cell>
						<text code>ui.theme</>
					</>
				</>
				<row>
					<cell>
						<text code>themes/&lt;name&gt;.css</>
					</>
					<cell>one of Spell's own themes, on top of <text code>classic</></>
					<cell>
						<text code>ui.theme</>
					</>
				</>
				<row>
					<cell>
						<text code>ui.css</>
					</>
					<cell>one <text code>@import</> entry of the page set, for pages without the runtime</>
					<cell>--</>
				</>
			</>
			<markdown>
				\* Generated from `styles.en.ts` by `yarn gen:styles`, committed, so consumers need no build step.
				`spell/ui/styles` exports each sheet as text, plus `foundationCSS` (for the document AND every shadow root)
				and `pageCSS` (foundation + typography + native, for the document only).
			</>
		</>

		<section label="Layers" sticky="stack" collapsible dividing>
			<markdown>
				```css
				@layer ui.reset, ui.tokens, ui.base, ui.components, ui.utilities, ui.theme, ui.app;
				```
			</>
			<markdown>
				- Later layers win regardless of specificity; unlayered page CSS beats all of them.
				- Each component adds `ui.components.<name>.types / content / variations / states`, so states beat variations
				  without `!important`.
				- `layers.css` must be adopted FIRST into the document and into every shadow root (each is its own scope).
				- A theme sits in `ui.theme`, above every component layer; your own overrides go in `ui.app`, above the theme.
			</>
		</>

		<section label="Units" sticky="stack" collapsible dividing>
			<markdown>
				- NEVER `rem`: the host page can redefine it. The ONE absolute length is `--ui-font-size` (px, default `16px`);
				  everything else is `em` of the local font size, or px for hairlines and shadows.
				- A component root sets `font-size: calc(var(--ui-font-size) * var(--ui-scale, 1))` and uses `em` inside.
				- Scale a whole region by overriding `--ui-font-size` on a wrapper; components inside follow.
			</>

			<section label="Scaling a region" sticky collapsible dividing>
				<example "Scaling a region" description="Change `--ui-font-size` on a wrapper and everything inside follows.">
					<html>
						<ui-docs-tokens global playground tokens="--ui-font-size">
							<ui-header level="4">A header</ui-header>
							<ui-button color="primary">A button</ui-button>
							<ui-label>A label</ui-label>
							<ui-input placeholder="An input" aria-label="An input"></ui-input>
						</ui-docs-tokens>
					</html>
				</example>
			</>
		</>

		<section label="Remaps" sticky="stack" collapsible dividing>
			<markdown>
				Component CSS never names a hue. A colour class re-points the GENERIC tokens (`--ui-color`, `--ui-color-text` ...)
				and one rule set consumes them. Sizes work the same way, through `--ui-scale`.
			</>
			<markdown>
				```css
				/* generated, colors.css */
				.ui.red,
				.ui-red {
				  --ui-color: var(--ui-red);
				  --ui-color-text: var(--ui-red-text);
				  --ui-color-on: var(--ui-red-on); /* white or ink, picked for WCAG contrast when generated */
				}

				/* component CSS */
				.ui.button {
				  background: var(--ui-color, var(--_ui-button-background));
				  color: var(--ui-color-on, inherit);
				}
				```
			</>
			<markdown>
				- Components READ `--ui-color*` with a fallback for the uncoloured look; they NEVER declare them.
				- The generic tokens INHERIT: `class="ui-red"` on a wrapper recolours every component inside it.
				- `data-variation="red small"` (tooltips, popups) sets `--ui-variation-color` instead, so a coloured tooltip never
				  recolours the element it hangs off.
			</>

			<section label="A remapped region" sticky collapsible dividing>
				<example "A remapped region" description="`ui-violet` on a wrapper re-points `--ui-color`: the uncoloured components inside turn violet.">
					<stack class="ui-violet">
						<button>Button</button>
						<label>Label</label>
						<progress value="60" aria-label="Progress"/>
					</stack>
					<message slot="description" state="info" size="small">A plain element is the wrapper here: a coloured container component (<text code>&lt;ui-segment color&gt;</text>, a card, a message) resets the generic tokens for its content on purpose, so its own colour never leaks into what it holds.</message>
				</example>
			</>
		</>

		<section label="Component tokens" sticky collapsible dividing>
			<markdown>
				Every component has public tokens of its own, `--ui-<component>-*` (`--ui-button-radius`, `--ui-card-width`), one
				per Fomantic `.variables` entry that still matters, listed with their defaults on its page's Theming tab. Set them
				anywhere above or on the component:
			</>
			<table celled padding="compact">
				<row header>
					<cell>Where</>
					<cell>Reaches</>
					<cell>Example</>
				</>
				<row>
					<cell><text code>:root</> or a theme sheet</>
					<cell>every instance on the page</>
					<cell>
						<text code>:root &#123; --ui-button-radius: 0 &#125;</>
					</>
				</>
				<row>
					<cell>any ancestor</>
					<cell>a region</>
					<cell>
						<text code>.toolbar &#123; --ui-button-padding-inline: 0.75em &#125;</>
					</>
				</>
				<row>
					<cell>the host</>
					<cell>one kind, or one instance</>
					<cell>
						<text code>ui-button.cta &#123; ... &#125;</>
					</>
				</>
				<row>
					<cell>
						<text code>::part(&lt;root part&gt;)</>
					</>
					<cell>the inner box itself</>
					<cell>
						<text code>ui-button::part(button) &#123; --ui-button-radius: 0 &#125;</>
					</>
				</>
				<row>
					<cell>the app stylesheet</>
					<cell>the inner box, by class grammar</>
					<cell>
						<text code>.ui.primary.button &#123; --ui-button-radius: 0 &#125;</>
					</>
				</>
			</>
			<markdown>
				```css
				/* every button */
				:root { --ui-button-radius: 0; }
				/* a region */
				.toolbar { --ui-button-padding-inline: 0.75em; }
				/* one kind, on its inner box */
				ui-button.cta::part(button) { --ui-button-background: gold; }
				/* the headers inside every card (an owner token) */
				ui-card { --ui-card-header-color: var(--ui-violet-text); }
				```
			</>
			<markdown>
				- They inherit into the shadow root, where the component reads each one through a private alias
				  (`--_ui-button-radius: var(--ui-button-radius, var(--ui-radius))`), so nothing inside blocks them.
				- A variation that SWAPS a value (`circular`) wins over the token; one derived from it (`compact` padding)
				  follows it. Restyle a swapping variation with plain properties:
				  `ui-button[appearance~="circular"]::part(button) { border-radius: 0.5em }`.
				- Never set the `--_ui-*` names: they are the components' private plumbing.
			</>
		</>

		<section label="The app stylesheet" sticky collapsible dividing>
			<markdown>
				Fomantic's `.overrides` files have one home here: the page's ONE `<link>` or `<style>` with
				`id="ui-app-stylesheet"`. The runtime mirrors it into a shared constructable sheet and appends it LAST to every
				component's `adoptedStyleSheets`, so its rules reach component internals in Fomantic's class grammar. Later edits,
				a late insertion and `<link>` loads are picked up.
			</>
			<markdown>
				```css
				/* #ui-app-stylesheet */
				@layer ui.app {
				  .ui.primary.button {
				    border-radius: var(--ui-radius-pill);
				  }
				  .ui.card > .content > .header {
				    letter-spacing: 0.01em;
				  }
				}
				```
			</>
			<markdown>
				This site's own stylesheet is its app stylesheet: every site rule is a `.site-*` class, so none matches inside a
				component by accident.
			</>
		</>

		<section label="Overriding colours" sticky collapsible dividing>
			<markdown>
				- Globally: one base token re-colours a hue everywhere, derived states and roles included (see Sitewide defaults).
				- One role of one hue: `:root { --ui-yellow-text: oklch(0.62 0.13 80) }` (themes do this, e.g. classic's yellow
				  text).
				- Per region: tokens inherit, so override them on a wrapper: `<section style="--ui-font-size: 18px; --ui-radius: 0">`.
				- Per instance: set the generic tokens on an UNCOLOURED component; they inherit into its shadow. Set
				  `--ui-color-on` whenever you set `--ui-color` (it's never derived), and don't combine it with `color="..."`.
			</>
			<markdown>
				```html
				<ui-button style="--ui-color: hotpink; --ui-color-hover: deeppink; --ui-color-on: black">Hot</ui-button>
				```
			</>
			<message state="warning" size="small">
				<markdown>
					Re-pointing a BASE on an intermediate element (`.card { --ui-red: hotpink }`) changes `--ui-red` below it, but
					not the derived `--ui-red-hover` / `-text`: custom properties substitute `var()` where they're declared, at
					`:root`. Override `--ui-color*` there instead, or the base on `:root`.
				</>
			</>
		</>
	</>

	<section label="Cascading inheritance">
		<markdown>
			Fomantic resolves a variable through three levels: its defaults, a packaged theme, then your site theme. Ours is
			the same idea in CSS layers and custom properties, so each later level only says what it changes:
		</>
		<steps direction="vertical" ordered>
			<step icon="lock" heading="Foundation" description="tokens.css, colors.css:  ui.tokens"/>
			<step icon="download" heading="Packaged theme" description="classic + one of Spell's themes:  ui.theme"/>
			<step icon="user" heading="Your site" description="tokens and the app stylesheet:  ui.app"/>
		</>

		<section label="Foundation tokens" sticky collapsible dividing>
			<markdown>
				The defaults every theme starts from: declared on `:root`, plus a `:host` copy guarded by a style query, so a
				component rendered without the page sheet still gets them, while page and wrapper overrides inherit everywhere
				else. Colours are `light-dark()` streams; the per-scheme bases (`--ui-red-on-light`, `--ui-red-on-dark`) are
				registered with `@property`, so they animate. Each colour swatch below is live: it follows the theme and scheme.
			</>
			<html>
				<ui-docs-tokens global></>
			</>
		</>

		<section label="Colour tokens" sticky="stack" collapsible dividing>
			<markdown>
				For every hue (`red orange yellow olive green teal blue violet purple pink brown grey black`), the aliases
				(`primary` => `blue`, `secondary` => `black`) and the semantic colours (`positive negative info warning`):
			</>
			<table celled padding="compact">
				<row header>
					<cell>Token</>
					<cell>Meaning</>
					<cell>Fomantic</>
				</>
				<row>
					<cell>
						<text code>--ui-red</>
					</>
					<cell>the colour, <text code>light-dark(var(--ui-red-on-light), var(--ui-red-on-dark))</></>
					<cell><text code>@red</> / <text code>@lightRed</></>
				</>
				<row>
					<cell>
						<text code>--ui-red-hover / -focus / -down / -active</>
					</>
					<cell>states (darken + saturate; <text code>black</> lightens)</>
					<cell><text code>@redHover</> ...</>
				</>
				<row>
					<cell>
						<text code>--ui-red-text / -header / -border / -background</>
					</>
					<cell>roles, per scheme</>
					<cell><text code>@redTextColor</> ...</>
				</>
				<row>
					<cell>
						<text code>--ui-red-inverted</>
					</>
					<cell>the colour on dark surfaces, whatever the scheme</>
					<cell>
						<text code>@lightRed</>
					</>
				</>
				<row>
					<cell><text code>--ui-red-on</> / <text code>--ui-red-inverted-on</></>
					<cell>text ON the solid colour (white or ink), per scheme, picked for WCAG AA 4.5:1</>
					<cell>
						<text code>@white</>
					</>
				</>
			</>
		</>
	</>

	<section label="Porting a Fomantic theme">
		<markdown>
			Fomantic's themes, ported this way, are archived now (`src/styles/themes/archive/`):  kept to copy from, in no
			menu and no bundle. They're DELTAS on its default look, and ours of that look is `classic.css`, so a ported theme is
			applied ON TOP of `classic`: both sheets, `classic` first, both in `@layer ui.theme`. A theme sheet never repeats
			classic's tokens and has two halves:

			1. TOKENS on `:root`: Fomantic's `.variables` as `--ui-*` globals and `--ui-<tag>-*` component tokens. They
			   inherit into shadow roots.
			2. OVERRIDES: Fomantic's `.overrides`, and any variable with no token, as CLASS-GRAMMAR rules (`.ui.button`,
			   `.ui.menu .item`) for the markup our components render INSIDE their shadow roots.

			References, in the archive: `github.css` (16 components, tokens + overrides), `material.css` (fonts, palette,
			`-on` re-checks), `fomantic-classic.css` (small, mostly overrides).
		</>
		<steps direction="vertical" ordered>
			<step heading="Read the theme" description="reference/Fomantic-UI/src/themes/<name>/**:  globals/site.variables first, then each component's .variables and .overrides.  Only what's there is the theme."/>
			<step heading="Create the sheet" description="themes/<name>.css with a header comment like github.css's (what, touches, font, dark scheme, NOT ported), all inside @layer ui.theme.  No registry edit:  UI.themes globs the folder."/>
			<step heading="Tokens first" description="On :root, from each component's token block or its docs table;  the mapping table below."/>
			<step heading="Overrides second" description="Fomantic's .overrides, and any variable with no token, as class-grammar rules with the selectors the component's own sheet uses."/>
			<step heading="Skip what can't be ported" description="List it in the header's NOT ported, and record a caveat."/>
			<step heading="Assets" description="Images or a font the theme really needs go in themes/<name>/, referenced relatively."/>
			<step heading="Test" description="A describe(\"<name>\") in the themes test (themes.test.ts):  at least one computed style per touched component, inside its shadow root."/>
			<step heading="Look" description="Screenshot the touched components with the theme applied, next to fomantic-ui.com's, light and dark."/>
		</>

		<section label="Variables to tokens" sticky collapsible dividing>
			<table celled padding="compact" appearance="striped">
				<row header>
					<cell>Fomantic</>
					<cell>Ours</>
					<cell>Note</>
				</>
				<row>
					<cell>
						<text code>@emSize</>
					</>
					<cell>
						<text code>--ui-font-size</>
					</>
					<cell>px; every <text code>em</> follows</>
				</>
				<row>
					<cell><text code>@pageFont</>, <text code>@fontName</> / <text code>@headerFont</></>
					<cell><text code>--ui-font-family</> / <text code>--ui-font-family-heading</></>
					<cell>load the font yourself</>
				</>
				<row>
					<cell><text code>@lineHeight</> / <text code>@headerLineHeight</></>
					<cell><text code>--ui-line-height</> / <text code>--ui-line-height-heading</></>
					<cell>unitless</>
				</>
				<row>
					<cell>
						<text code>@textColor</>
					</>
					<cell>
						<text code>--ui-ink-on-light</>
					</>
					<cell>text roles are alphas of the ink</>
				</>
				<row>
					<cell>
						<text code>@pageBackground</>
					</>
					<cell>
						<text code>--ui-background</>
					</>
					<cell><text code>light-dark()</> pair</>
				</>
				<row>
					<cell><text code>@borderColor</> / <text code>@internalBorderColor</> / <text code>@selectedBorderColor</></>
					<cell><text code>--ui-border-color</> / <text code>-internal</> / <text code>-selected</></>
					<cell/>
				</>
				<row>
					<cell><text code>@defaultBorderRadius</>, <text code>@absoluteBorderRadius</></>
					<cell><text code>--ui-radius-s</> / <text code>-m</> / <text code>-l</></>
					<cell/>
				</>
				<row>
					<cell>
						<text code>@disabledOpacity</>
					</>
					<cell>
						<text code>--ui-disabled-opacity</>
					</>
					<cell/>
				</>
				<row>
					<cell><text code>@red</> ... / <text code>@lightRed</> ...</>
					<cell><text code>--ui-red-on-light</> / <text code>--ui-red-on-dark</></>
					<cell>OKLCH; re-check <text code>--ui-red-on</></>
				</>
				<row>
					<cell>
						<text code>@primaryColor: @green</>
					</>
					<cell><text code>--ui-primary: var(--ui-green)</> + <text code>-inverted</>, <text code>-on</>, <text code>-inverted-on</></>
					<cell>states and roles derive</>
				</>
				<row>
					<cell><text code>@linkColor</> / <text code>@linkHoverColor</></>
					<cell><text code>--ui-link</> / <text code>--ui-link-hover</></>
					<cell/>
				</>
				<row>
					<cell><text code>@infoTextColor</>, <text code>@infoBorderColor</>, <text code>@infoBackgroundColor</> ...</>
					<cell><text code>--ui-info-text</> / <text code>-border</> / <text code>-background</></>
					<cell><text code>error</> is <text code>negative</></>
				</>
				<row>
					<cell>
						<text code>@relativeNpx</>
					</>
					<cell><text code>N / &lt;emSize&gt;</> em, e.g. <text code>0.6154em</> (8px at 13px)</>
					<cell>NEVER <text code>rem</></>
				</>
				<row>
					<cell><text code>Nrem</>, a fixed <text code>Npx</> that should follow the size</>
					<cell><text code>calc(var(--ui-font-size) * N)</> or <text code>* N / &lt;emSize&gt;</></>
					<cell/>
				</>
				<row>
					<cell><text code>@verticalPadding</> / <text code>@horizontalPadding</></>
					<cell><text code>--ui-&lt;tag&gt;-padding-block</> / <text code>-inline</> (or one <text code>-padding</>)</>
					<cell/>
				</>
				<row>
					<cell><text code>@backgroundColor</>, <text code>@hoverBackgroundColor</> ...</>
					<cell><text code>--ui-&lt;tag&gt;-background</> / <text code>-hover</> / <text code>-down</> / <text code>-active</></>
					<cell/>
				</>
				<row>
					<cell>
						<text code>@boxShadow</>
					</>
					<cell><text code>--ui-&lt;tag&gt;-shadow</> where the family has one</>
					<cell>else an override</>
				</>
				<row>
					<cell>
						<text code>@borderRadius</>
					</>
					<cell>
						<text code>--ui-&lt;tag&gt;-radius</>
					</>
					<cell/>
				</>
				<row>
					<cell><text code>@fontWeight</>, <text code>@textTransform</></>
					<cell><text code>--ui-&lt;tag&gt;-font-weight</> ... where it exists</>
					<cell>else an override</>
				</>
			</>
			<markdown>
				- Colours as OKLCH, as `light-dark(<Fomantic's>, <the default dark recipe>)` where the default is a pair: keep
				  dark mode working (Fomantic had none). Copy the dark half from `colors.css` / `classic.css`.
				- A token holding a `background` may take a gradient when the sheet paints it with the `background` shorthand.
				- Changed a hue's base? Re-check its `--ui-<hue>-on`: white if it reaches 4.5:1 on the colour, else
				  `var(--ui-ink-on-light)`.
			</>
		</>

		<section label="Overrides" sticky="stack" collapsible dividing>
			<markdown>
				- Use the selectors the COMPONENT'S sheet uses for that box (its header's "Shadow markup contract"). An item box
				  often has two, the element's (`:host(:state(in-menu)) > .item`) and static class grammar (`.ui.menu .item`):
				  write both. `<ui-table>` renders a light-DOM `<table>`: `:is(.ui.table, :where(ui-table) > table)`.
				- `ui.theme` beats EVERY component layer, variations and states included. Fomantic's overrides competed by
				  specificity, so scope yours to what they meant: `.ui.button:not(.basic, .inverted, .tertiary)`, not `.ui.button`.
				- Re-colour one component only by writing the remap on its box:
				  `.ui.button:is(.primary, .blue) { --ui-color: ...; --ui-color-on: ... }`; hover and down states derive.
				- Don't set private tokens (`--_ui-*`); querying a private SWITCH is fine:
				  `@container style(--_ui-steps-layout: horizontal) { ... }`.
				- `!important` in Fomantic: usually unnecessary here (the layer already wins); drop it.
			</>
		</>

		<section label="What can't be ported" sticky collapsible dividing>
			<markdown>
				- Icon FONTS: icons are SVG packs; build a pack instead (see [Icons](/icons)).
				- `@import (css) url(...)` of web fonts: a runtime sheet drops `@import`; the page loads fonts.
				- Breakpoints (`@mobileBreakpoint` ...) and `@pageMinWidth`: build-time `@custom-media` and page layout.
				- Per-component SIZE ladders in px / rem: sizes are ratios of `--ui-font-size`; scale the default instead.
				- Markup we don't render: a component we don't have, Fomantic's JS-added classes like `.focused` (try the native
				  state, e.g. `:focus-within`).
			</>
		</>
	</>

	<section label="Build notes">
		<markdown>
			- `@custom-media` and the `@import`s in the sheets need Lightning CSS (Vite's `css.transformer: "lightningcss"`
			  with `drafts.customMedia`); raw, those rules are dropped.
			- `css.lightningcss.targets` MUST be modern browsers. With Vite's default targets Lightning CSS lowers
			  `light-dark()` into variables substituted at `:root`, which breaks `ui-dark` subtrees.
		</>
	</>
</page>
